# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Source data for the build scripts, not the build output. The raw FAA NASR
# cycle is ~1 GB and is reissued every 28 days; `data/aero/airports.sqlite`
# is the 3 MB artefact built from it and *is* committed, since that is what
# the app ships with offline.
.cache/
data/nasr/

# FAA raster charts are downloaded by hand into data/charts/<sectional|tac>/
# (see data/charts/README.txt). At 30-80 MB each the source GeoTIFFs stay
# out of the repo -- everything one level under data/charts/ is one FAA
# download and is ignored. Re-download them when a cycle lapses.
data/charts/*/
!data/charts/README.txt

# Except the rendered tiles, which *are* committed, for the same reason
# data/aero/airports.sqlite is: they are the build output the app ships
# with, and the only form in which a chart reaches a browser anywhere but
# this desktop. A deployed instance has no GeoTIFFs and not enough memory
# to decode one, so committing the tiles is what lets it serve a chart with
# no build step at all. Rebuild with `make charts`.
#
# Only `make charts` writes here. Tiles the dev server renders as you pan --
# thousands of them, at zooms past the committed cap -- go to
# .cache/chart-tiles/ instead, ignored by the .cache/ rule above. Were both
# kinds in this folder git could not tell them apart, and `git add` of it
# would commit whatever the last browsing session happened to look at.
!data/charts/tiles/
